ies. It distributes its products and services through corporate and franchise locations. Goosehead Insurance, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Westlake, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark K. Miller CPA | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $228K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 29%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $54K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Goosehead Insurance, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $2.0B market cap on $365M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 35% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 25-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $86M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -15.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 11.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 45% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.44705181299110214},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Goosehead Insurance (GSHD) Rebounds Sharply, Is The Stock A Bargain?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-gshd/goosehead-insurance/news/goosehead-insurance-gshd-rebounds-sharply-is-the-stock-a-bar","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793953681.491,"origin":"ti